{"author":{"id":"aefab16712695e4f092f7bad7c1285ac48ce0d1ef6cc283cea20b3795ed9457a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788764493,"nonce":"wwx7IRsQ2HQ8fgnKlxXkqgSuB9c=","title":"[SDK Bug] collab keepalive wakes subagent instead of notifying live master","message":"Reproduction: register a managed subagent with parent as live master and a working/assigned task; let subagent pane transition to Waiting. Current behavior: src/server/keepalive.rs tick_with iterates workers with actionable tasks, sees idle pane, and creates a keepalive Message addressed to the subagent peer plus a tmux wake. The subagent never accepts task-keepalive notices (managed subagents use ready/working only), so it never rearms and never closes the task. Result: the subagent keeps being woken, master has no signal, status column stays ambiguous between working and idle, tokens are wasted and the task can never reach merged/closed without manual master force-close. Expected: keepalive must (a) update Subagent.status to idle|working based on probe, (b) send a single durable subagent-status message to the parent master) not the subagent, (c) never create a keepalive Message or tmux wake targeted at the subagent peer. Same fix applies to ordinary workers but with worker-targeted keeps; the fix path is managed subagent only.","files":null}]}